  "body": "The parent #4365 is merged (`75e9b0ad7`); this PR now shows only its own commits.\n\n## What changed\n\nU9 of #3663: the tool list of the tool library window. The page sits inside the frame of #4365. Only the tool list page changes (its \"My library\" source included); `frame.rs` does not change.\n\n- **One header row:** the source tabs (Document, My library, Catalog, in the mockup order), one search box, then **New tool…**, **Import…** and **Export…** at the right.\n- **Import…** opens a menu with the import mode (#899), \"Import tool holders\" (#889) and \"Choose a library file…\". A click on a mode or the check box keeps the menu open. No option is lost.\n- **Search:** one box with the placeholder \"Filter by name, diameter or part number\" (AccessKit name \"Search tools\"). The text splits into terms, and each term must match (AND): \"6 ball\" finds the 6 mm ball nose mills.\n  - A text term matches the name, the type, the category, the holder, the part number or the vendor (#898).\n  - A number matches the cutting or shank diameter within 0.05 mm, in the document unit. It also matches the tool number, and the text when it has 4 or more characters (a numeric part number). \"T5\" matches tool number 5.\n  - The search works the same in Document, My library (component rows) and Catalog. The text holds when the source changes.\n  - \"N of M tools\" (\"N of M components\") heads the rows. Esc clears the box.\n- **Category rail:** it lists every category of each group. The count is the count of the rows that match the search.\n- **Columns:** drawing, T, Name, Type, Ø, Flute, Flutes, Holder, Gauge, **Recipes** (count), and the **in document** mark on Catalog and My library rows. The heads carry the unit (\"Ø mm\"). A click on a Document row's name opens the tool in the editor.\n- **Frame cost:** State keeps the rows and the hits (`state_tool_list.rs`, built by `tool_library_dialog/list_rows.rs`). The rows are read once for each document version. The hits are built again only when the rows, the text or the unit change. A still frame builds nothing; a counter test pins this.\n- The Tool type combo is gone: the rail and the search do its work. `State::tool_catalog_kind` and `ComponentsView::filter` are removed; `tool_catalog_name` is now `tool_search`.\n- The decisions are in `docs/decisions/4335-tool-list-search.md`.\n\nNew files: `tool_library_dialog/list_header.rs`, `list_rows.rs`, `search.rs`, `crates/ui/src/state_tool_list.rs`, and the test module `tests/tool_library_search.rs`. All are in `crates/ui`; no new crate dependency.\n\n## Screenshots\n\nBefore: the head of #4365 (its \"after\" image). After: this head, 1920 × 1080, the seeded document with four tools in a BT40 ER32 holder.\n\n| | Image |\n|---|---|\n| Before (#4365) | ![before](https://raw.githubusercontent.com/qsmits/Camcraft/pr-screenshots/4365/after/1-tool-list.png) |\n| After: Document | ![after](https://raw.githubusercontent.com/qsmits/Camcraft/pr-screenshots/4381/after-document.png) |\n| After: Catalog, \"6 ball\" | ![after](https://raw.githubusercontent.com/qsmits/Camcraft/pr-screenshots/4381/after-catalog-search.png) |\n| After: My library | ![after](https://raw.githubusercontent.com/qsmits/Camcraft/pr-screenshots/4381/after-my-library.png) |\n| After: the Import… menu | ![after](https://raw.githubusercontent.com/qsmits/Camcraft/pr-screenshots/4381/after-import-menu.png) |\n| After the merge of `main` (U10, U11), 1280 × 720: Document | ![after merge](https://raw.githubusercontent.com/qsmits/Camcraft/pr-screenshots/4381/after-merge-document.png) |\n| After the merge of `main` (U10, U11), 1280 × 720: Catalog, \"6 ball\" | ![after merge](https://raw.githubusercontent.com/qsmits/Camcraft/pr-screenshots/4381/after-merge-catalog-search.png) |\n\n## Tests\n\nPinning tests (new):\n\n- `egui_app::tests::tool_library_search::catalog_search_by_one_term_two_terms_a_diameter_no_match_and_esc`\n- `egui_app::tests::tool_library_search::document_search_by_name_type_diameter_part_number_no_match_and_esc`\n- `egui_app::tests::tool_library_search::my_library_search_by_name_two_terms_no_match_and_esc`\n- `egui_app::tests::tool_library_search::the_search_box_has_its_name_and_placeholder_and_holds_between_sources`\n- `egui_app::tests::tool_library_search::a_still_frame_builds_no_hits_and_a_change_builds_once` (the frame-cost counter test)\n- `egui_app::tool_library_dialog::search::tests::*` (4 matcher tests: AND, the diameter tolerance in mm and inch, the tool number and the part number, the empty query)\n\nUpdated: `layout_window_tool_library` now asserts the one header row (left to right, one row), the count between the header and the column heads, and the column heads left to right. The issue names it `layout_page_tool_library`; the window keeps its `layout_window_` name (AGENTS.md: `layout_window_<window>`). Also updated for the new labels: `catalog_filters` (the rail replaces the type combo), `edm_tool_visibility`, `tool_undercut`, `tool_icon_wiring`, `tool_library_import` (the check box is in the Import… menu), `tool_properties`, `tool_library_mockup`, `layout_window_tool_editor`, `layout_window_my_library`.\n\n`#[test]` count of `crates/ui`: 1961 before, 1970 after. After the merge of `main` with U10 and U11: 1991 on `main`, 2000 on this branch (+9). No test is deleted or ignored. No snapshot PNG changes.\n\n## Gate\n\nBase: `b1365b233f77c1b9c5b41d1db865e565e23eff5e` (the head of #4365).\n\n- `cargo xtask gate quick --base b1365b233…` on head cfdb27889: 18 steps, 0 failed (ui build, ui suites: lib and the 16 ui integration suites).\n- `cargo clippy -p camcraft-ui --all-targets -- -D warnings`: clean on head cfdb27889.\n- Light lane: not run. The diff touches only `crates/ui`; the light twins are in `camcraft-motion` and `camcraft-app`, which do not depend on `crates/ui` (`cargo xtask gate light --dry-run` lists 6 motion and app steps). The reviewer runs it if needed.\n\n## Not exercised\n\n- The native file dialogs of Import and Export (the buttons call the same `State` functions as before).\n- The browser build (the file buttons keep the same browser refusals).\n- An inch document in the UI: the matcher tests cover inch numbers; no UI test switches the unit.\n\nChangelog: The tool library list has one header row with one search box (name, type, diameter, holder, tool number, part number and vendor), \"N of M tools\", every category in the rail, and Recipes and \"in document\" columns.\n\nEffort: medium\n\nFixes #4335\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n\n\n",
